<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42167" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sācōmārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		sacoma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>serving for a counterpoise</i>, <i>used for a weight in a balance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cucurbitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. in Jon. 4, 6</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sācōmārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>one who makes
				counterpoises</i> or <i>weights</i> in gen.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">called also PONDERARIVS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4274</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sācōmārĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n., <i>the public
				balance</i> or <i>weighing place</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4109</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">7194</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
